  "body": "A dead-end later Outside pass now enters by a ramp along the pass, so the later pass starts in cleared stock.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_order.rs`: `lead_in` searched only 0.9 tool radii. Each later pass starts at a dead end one stepover (4.00 mm) from the nearest cut walk. The new entry ramps along the pass at a dead end, at 3 degrees.\n- The incompleteness guard (`unswept`, `LEFT_TOL` 0.1 mm2) and the `RINGS_FALLBACK` warning stay. No refusal is changed. The removed `PassStart::rank` and the parallel `sided_rings` planner are not re-added.\n\n## The pin\n\n`outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` (100 x 40 band, radius 15, 2D Offset Outside, 0.25 mm material grid, 3 tool radii of floor feed after the first land):\n\n- Red on main `4c0a157e1`: 332.88 mm2 of uncut stock.\n- Green on this head: 0.00 mm2.\n\n## Readings\n\n`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3`, `-j 3`, no sccache:\n\n- motion `pass_start_engagement`, `pass_start_levels`, and the lib `machining2d` tests: green.\n- app `offset_pass_start` and app `example_catalog`: green.\n- motion clippy: clean.\n- The full `cargo xtask gate quick` was stopped at the tier change and has no final verdict.\n\n## Tier note\n\nThe fix came from an `issue-worker-high` worker while the issue was claimed at `effort:max` (the claim predates the label change). The claim of the earlier `issue-worker-max` worker is released: its worktree and its commit are gone. The surviving fix is branch `issue/3567-ramp-entry-at-dead-end` at `e7ae538a3`. The review runs at the `effort:max` tier.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset Outside: a later pass that starts at a dead end now enters by a 3-degree ramp along the pass, so the entry starts in cleared stock and leaves no uncut band.\n\nFixes #3567\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
